  "lessons": [
    {
      "title": "intro",
      "slug": "intro",
      "displayOrder": 1,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 563,
        "lessonOrder": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\n\t.container-border {\r\n\t\tborder: 1px solid #ccc;\r\n\t\tborder-radius: 15px;\r\n\t\tpadding-top: 20px;\r\n\t\tpadding-right: 20px;\r\n\t\tpadding-bottom: 20px;\r\n\t\tpadding-left: 20px;\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\thr.style13 {\r\n\t\theight: 10px;\r\n\t\tborder: 0;\r\n\t\tbox-shadow: 0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset;\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n\t\r\n\r\n\t\tFinishing round necklines is always a challenge for knitters. Neckbands add the finishing touch to your sweaters. No part of the sweater is more visible, so it's important to master the ART of knitting bands.\r\n\t\t<ul class=\"fa-ul\">\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>We're picking up stitches along a round shape</li><br>\r\n\t\t\t<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>The neckline consists of both stitches and rows</li><br>\r\n\t\t\t<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>The neckline needs to stay stretchy to fit over the head (for a pullover)</li><br>\r\n\t\t\t<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span>Keeping the band flat against the body is the goal for a professional finish</li><br>\r\n\t\t</ul>\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\r\n\t<div class=\"text-center\"><span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em\">\"Finishing necklines<br> is an ART<br> not a science.\"</span></div>\r\n\r\nI want you to take time to practice some of these techniques BEFORE putting a lot of time into a full sweater. The confidence you gain will go a long way to success with EVERY sweater you knit in the future.<br>\r\n<h1>Options:</h1><br>\r\n<b>The focus of this knit-along is round neck FINISHING. We will be exploring different band finishes.<br> If you aren't comfortable with shaping necklines, please take time to practice first.</b><br><mark>To save time and focus on neck bands, I suggest trying Cut 'n Sew. Even if you would never use this method on a \"real\" sweater. It will give you the opportunity to spend your knit-along time working with bands. The techniques we will cover can be used for both shaped and cut 'n sew methods.<br>\r\n\r\n\t<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\t\r\n\t\t<div class=\"container-border\">\r\n\r\n\t\t\t<h3>Need practice with Cut 'n Sew?<br></h3>\r\n\t\t\t<br> Previous Knit-along:<b>Fearless Cut 'n Sew finishing</b> <small><em>Free for subscribers</em></small><br><center><a href=\"/knitclub/71/Knitalong/fearless-cut-n-sew-finishing\"> <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/93//v2/71/cut_n_sew_KAL.png\" width=\"200\"></a><br><div class=\"text-center\"></div>\r\n\t\t\t</center>\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t<div class=\"container-border\">\r\n\t\t\t<h3>Need practice perfecting shaped necklines? </h3>\r\n\t\t\t<br>Previous Knit-along: <b>Neckbands and Collars</b> <small><em>Free for subscribers</em></small><br><center><a href=\"/knitclub/77/Knitalong/neckbands-and-collars\"> <img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/93//v2/77/collars.png\" width=\"200\"></a><br><div class=\"text-center\"></div>\r\n\r\n\t\t\t</center>\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n\r\n\t\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 6629,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Introduction",
          "slug": "introduction",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 4375,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\nhr.style13 {\r\nheight: 10px;\r\nborder: 0;\r\nbox-shadow: 0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset;\r\n}\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em\">If you are new:</span><br>\r\n <b>Start small and gain confidence. Work the exercises in order, focusing on:<br></b><br>\r\n<ul class=\"fa-ul li_7px\">\r\n<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span> Neat Pickup with no holes or gathers</li>\r\n<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span> Picking up the right number of stitches for a neckband that lays flat with no puckering or ripples</li>\r\n<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span> Neat, secure finishing for a long-wearing sweater</li>\r\n<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span> For your first practice, consider knitting a single round front (as one side of a cardigan) instead of an entire sweater front</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em\">If you've \"been there .... done that\":</span><br>\r\n<b>Try something new!</b><br>\r\n<ul class=\"fa-ul li_7px\">\r\n<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span> Try a new-to-you technique</li>\r\n<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span> Incorporate a stitch pattern</li>\r\n<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span> Challenge yourself and knit a front and back sample, practicing joining 1 shoulder, adding the band and neatly joining the other shoulder and band.\r\n<li><span class=\"fa-li\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"></i></span> Put your ribber to work</li>\r\n</ul><br>\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">",
              "legacyComponentId": 6631,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "exerciseAccordion",
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "Knit and measure an accurate swatch",
                  "bodyHtml": "No matter what you want to knit, <b>knitting a gauge swatch is NOT OPTIONAL!</b><br>Without knowing gauge:<ul>\r\n\t<li>How do you know how much yarn you need?</li>\r\n\t<li>How are you going to know if the finished item will fit?</li>\r\n\t<li>Determine if you are even going to LIKE the resulting fabric</li>\r\n\t<li>Try out the chosen stitch pattern, maybe it's too tedious... learn this BEFORE starting to knit</li>\r\n\t<li>Dress the swatch and check for shrinkage, pilling, fading</li>\r\n\t<li>Save time by knowing AHEAD if the yarn will knit easily</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n\t<img src=\"/path/images/87/measure_rows.jpg\">\r\n\t<img src=\"/path/images/87/measure_stitches.jpg\">\r\n",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/93/arrow1.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Decisions, Decisions, Decisions",
                  "bodyHtml": "<ul>\r\n<li>Cut 'n Sew or Shaped neckline?</li>\r\n<li>Practice with just a front, or with both front and back?\r\n<li>Single bed neckband or ribber?</li>\r\n<li>Are you ready to add stitch patterning?</li>\r\n</ul>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/93/arrow2.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Shaping your neckline? Here's a practice pattern",
                  "bodyHtml": " <i class=\"fa fa-question-circle\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <a data-vimeoid=\"402313052\" class=\"videopopup\"> Are you new to Knit it Now Patterns? </a><br><a href=\"/knit/DynamicPattern/679/practice-necklines\"><img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/93/practice_necklines.jpg\" width=\"300\">\r\n</a>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/93/arrow3.png"
                },
                {
                  "title": "Try more than one band method",
                  "bodyHtml": "If you are new to necklines, Knit a One-Piece neckline and perfect the picking, grading and finishing techniques.<br>\r\nOnce you gain confidence try other techniques. \r\n<br><b>The more time you devote to this, the better your finishing will be.</b>",
                  "iconSrc": "/challenge/images/v2/93/arrow4.png"
                }
              ],
              "legacy": {
                "showText": "below",
                "size": null
              },
              "legacyComponentId": 6632,
              "order": 2
            }
